WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Democrats are in
messaging mode right now.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.204
So they're going to
fight Republicans

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.705
in the House on
everything we do,

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
because in the House
is the only place

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:09.809 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Republicans
have national power.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.011
We don't have it in the Senate.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.379
We don't have it
in the White House.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:15.248 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they're in 2024
presidential campaign mode.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:19.552 align:start position:0%
So Hakeem Jeffries, the minority
leader with the Democrats,

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:23.023 align:start size:97% position:3%
he calls us extreme MAGA
Republicans every single day.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.491
AOC calls us fascist

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.659
and every other name
that she can think of.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.328
Although I would say

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.097
people should really
pay attention to AOC.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.766
She's the true fascist.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.367
You see, what fascism is,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.237
is it's that, I call
it the unholy union

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.974
of big corporations
and big government,

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:43.843 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they have completely
aligned together,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.478
and it hurts the little people,

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:50.083 align:start size:97% position:3%
the little people that she
claims to protect and support.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.786
(cerebral music)

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.825
- I'm Dave Rubin,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.593
and joining me today
is the Congresswoman

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.430 align:start size:84% position:16%
representing Georgia's
14th District,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
Congresswoman Marjorie
Taylor Greene.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.032
Welcome to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.200
- Thank you, it's
good to be here.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.435
- I am glad to have you.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.502
I said to you right
before we started,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.970
we've got some poles up here

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I thought maybe you
could do some pull-ups from,

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.909
because you're always doing
exercise on the Capitol.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.510
Should we start that way
with a couple pull-ups?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.745
Or maybe we'll finish that way.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:81% position:19%
- We can finish
that way. (laughs)

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.047
- We'll finish that way.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.248
So, you know, it's funny,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.550
I've never sat down
with you before,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.984 align:start size:81% position:19%
and I'm sitting
down with probably

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
about 15 or 20 Congress people
and senators, et cetera,

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.591
and people think of you
as very controversial.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.860
And so I was like, all right,
I really want to figure out

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.863
what is truly like
the position you hold

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.598
that is the most controversial.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:42.001
And I really couldn't
come up with that much.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.703
So maybe we start there.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:88% position:13%
What do you make of
that notion in general?

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.208
- Well, it seems to
be in Washington DC,

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you come in very
convicted in your beliefs

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
and really represent
your district

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.247
and the beliefs that
your district hold,

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:58.251
you know, things like secure
borders, a strong economy,

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.688 align:start size:97% position:3%
freedom of speech, protecting
our Second Amendment,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.623
say no more foreign wars,

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's focus on America
and America first,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.262
being unapologetic
about being pro-life,

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.599
wanting to protect children
that seem to be under attack

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start size:88% position:13%
from these gender
lies, things like that,

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:20.073 align:start position:0%
Washington DC and the
mainstream media labels extreme,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:23.143
but actually in real America,
you know, Northwest Georgia,

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:25.578
where I come from, and pretty
much all across the country,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.714 align:start size:84% position:16%
those types of things
are not extreme.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.217
It's more Washington DC's
position that is extreme.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.319
- Do you sense that maybe
some of that is shifting?

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start position:0%
I sat down yesterday with
Speaker McCarthy at the Capitol,

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.757
and he was talking
about the agenda

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sort of the new
Republicans that are here,

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:42.495 align:start position:0%
and there does seem to be a
better messaging at the moment.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.097
It's partly why I'm
here for three days

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.798
to talk to all of you guys,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.700
because it does seem
like something's a
little bit different

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.270
than say the Republican
of 5 or 10 years ago.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:54.741
- Yes, and I think I can say
I've played a role in that.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.677
That was one of my objectives
when I came to Washington,

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.812
was to change the
Republican party.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:88% position:13%
You see, I was a
regular American, never
had run for office,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.551
wasn't involved in
politics at all,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:07.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was very upset with
the Republican party.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.222
I was a Republican voter,

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.391 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I didn't feel
like the Republicans

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
in Washington
reflected our values.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.895
And so, since I've
come to Washington,

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:20.300
I've never backed down on the
messaging that I've brought,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.101
the bills that I've introduced,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:97% position:3%
but also having communication
within our conference.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.773
Sometimes it's been arguments,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, it's
been confrontation.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.044
At times, it's been explanations

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.113
and really good
conversations of,

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.183 align:start size:97% position:3%
here's where our Republican
party needs to move to.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
This will reflect our
voters across the country

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.821
and then really be good
for our country overall.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
I supported Kevin McCarthy
in the Speaker's race

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.861
because I spent a lot of time
talking with him ahead of time

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:51.798
about what his goals were,
what his objectives were,

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:55.535
and also I developed a
relationship with him

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
and was really glad
that he listened to me

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.207
and the things that
were important for
my district as well.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.875 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Was it funny how that
whole thing was working out

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:88% position:13%
in the strange
bedfellows that created,

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it was like
Trump was supporting him,

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.114
you were supporting him,

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.849
Gates, who obviously you're in
line with on a lot of things,

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.484
was not supporting him.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.419
And then everybody was sort of,

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.988
the media was loving the fact

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:17.090 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you guys weren't
all walking in lockstep,

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.791 align:start size:84% position:16%
which actually I
tend to think is good

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.627 align:start size:88% position:13%
that people are
thinking for themselves,

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that it created all
of these odd relationships

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:24.497
that maybe didn't exist before.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.700
- Well, I think, what it did
is it pulled back the curtain

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.602
into the Republican conference,

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:33.706
and it showed different views
that the media didn't expect

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.408
and a lot of people, of course,

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.144
just watching from the
outside didn't expect.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.313
Over half of the Freedom Caucus,

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.315 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm a member of
the Freedom Caucus,

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.952 align:start position:0%
Over half of the Freedom Caucus
supported Kevin McCarthy,

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:48.454
myself, Jim Jordan, many others.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.623
But then some of
my best friends,

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.525
the people that I'm
always in line with,

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.260
they didn't, they opposed him.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.663
And then you saw the
debate back and forth,

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:57.897
sort of the internal war.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.466
But like I said, it
was all on display

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.769
on cameras, on C-SPAN,

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:06.205 align:start position:0%
and the media was front and
center, of course, enjoying it.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:07.540
Well, you wanna know why.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
The media really likes
to see Republicans

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
fight with each other?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:15.381 align:start size:97% position:3%
- But I have been calling
basic, our internal arguments,

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.917
I call 'em the civil
war within the party.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.019
And I think it's
good, I really do.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.155 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is what
Washington is about.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:25.358
It's a place where we
hammer out debates,

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:27.427
we discuss policy, and, yeah,

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:29.662
that means that we
argue sometimes.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:32.165 align:start size:84% position:16%
I never think
that's a bad thing.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.400
What we do have to do in
our conference though,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.770 align:start position:0%
is we worked it out, we elected
Kevin McCarthy as Speaker,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.238
we had our rules packaged.

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the same, literally
the same from day one

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.911
to the last day,
only one change,

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.180
to motion to vacate the chair

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
went from five
members to one member.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.117 align:start size:88% position:13%
That was the only change
in the rules package.

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:54.053
But what we had to do is
we had to say, all right,

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.356 align:start position:0%
now that we've been through
this, we have to come together.

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.758
'Cause there's only
222 Republicans,

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:03.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
takes 218 to pass anything
on the House floor.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.365
And we have big battles ahead.

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.267
We have the budget, we've
got the debt ceiling fight,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.703 align:start size:81% position:19%
where we are gonna
have the NDAA.

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:12.705
We've got big things
that we have to do.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:13.906
We don't control the Senate,

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we don't control
the White House.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.410
So it's some challenges ahead.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.278
- So speaking of those
numbers in the Senate,

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.947
one of the things that
you guys just did pass

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:23.583 align:start size:88% position:13%
is this parental rights
and education bill.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.818 align:start size:84% position:16%
And as a Floridian,
I am well aware

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.588
of a little transparency
in education, obviously.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:32.158
Were you shocked that not one
Democrat signed this thing?

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:36.262 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, all it is
about is basically
that you gotta sign up.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.364 align:start position:0%
Like back in the day, third
grade, you're going to the zoo.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.199
Your parent has
to sign something

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.467
saying you're going to the zoo.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.669
I mean, it really, it's
just about transparency.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.838 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, no, they fought
us big time on it.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.407
When you're a father as well.

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.975
So I'm sure you appreciate it.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:51.043
And being from Florida,
you love your freedom.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.645
- [Dave] We do love our freedom.

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:54.313
- No, we fought the
Democrats on it.

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:57.316
And so the the things that
they said in the bill debate,

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.552
I actually presided in
the chair in some of it,

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:02.555 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then was paying close
attention to that committee.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:05.825 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were accusing
Republicans of banning books,

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:09.395 align:start size:84% position:16%
book burnings and
not teaching history.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.664
They even called us racists.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.066 align:start size:81% position:19%
They called us all
kinds of names,

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:16.536
when what we were really
saying is we want parents

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:20.940
to have the rights to have
control over curriculum,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.509
to be able to talk to
their school boards,

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
of course, have control
over their children

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.313
'cause they're the parents.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.781
And then the second piece there,

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:32.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're also the taxpayers
that fund the schools.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.253 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I think their voice
should be just as important.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.621
And all of us Republicans agreed

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:38.124
in spite of not one Democrat.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:41.093
- So when AOC basically
calls this thing fascist,

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:42.328
which she did on the floor,

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:45.198
and then, was it Hakeem
Jeffries, I think said

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:46.732
that they're not gonna
teach, they don't want,

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.435
the Republicans don't want
the Holocaust to be taught.

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.505
I'm guessing these guys don't
talk to you on the DL, right?

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:54.307 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like you're not
getting a lot of hellos

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.908 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the hallways
there and being like,

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:58.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Hey, guys, you
know, it's not true."

00:07:58.311 --> 00:08:00.780
- No, no, and, well, here's
the mode that they're in.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.381
So for people to understand,

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
Democrats are in
messaging mode right now.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.519
So they're going to
fight Republicans

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:07.987
in the House on everything we do

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:09.589 align:start size:84% position:16%
because in the House
is the only place

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.757 align:start size:84% position:16%
that Republicans
have national power.

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.092
We don't have it in the Senate.

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:14.460
We don't have it
in the White House.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.530 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they're in 2024
presidential campaign mode.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:21.234 align:start position:0%
So Hakeem Jeffries, the minority
leader with the Democrats,

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:25.338 align:start size:97% position:3%
he calls us extreme MAGA
Republicans every single day.

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:26.706
AOC calls us fascist

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:28.975
and every other name
that she can think of.

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.543
Although I would say

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:33.412
people should really
pay attention to AOC.

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:35.081
She's the true fascist.

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:36.616
You see what fascism is,

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:39.485
is it's that, I call
it the unholy union

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:43.623
of big corporations
and big government,

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:45.691 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they have completely
aligned together

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:47.760
and it hurts the little people,

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:51.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
the little people that she
claims to protect and support.

00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:55.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
Yeah, AOC's really the
fascist herself, and Hakeem-

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:56.235
- Isn't it funny that, I mean,

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.503
that's right outta
rules for radicals,

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.705
that you're supposed
to accuse the others

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.173
of what you are doing.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.942
- That's right, and they
do it, and they do it well.

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.644
Joe Biden's doing
it right now too.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:06.412
If people have been
paying attention,

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:08.948
he's tweeted out in the
past like week or so.

00:09:08.948 --> 00:09:11.651
He's blaming Republicans

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:14.854
for not wanting to
fund border security

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:17.156
to stop fentanyl from
coming in the country,

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:19.158
which is laughable,

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:22.995 align:start size:97% position:3%
because under Joe Biden,
we've seen fentanyl increase.

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:25.164
It's literally doubled
coming in the country.

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:28.701
And over 300 Americans
die every single day

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.670
