00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:00.366
It's sort of a weird state

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:01.701
in terms of making sense
of what's going on there.

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:02.735
What is that?

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:04.270
- Yeah.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.705
It's probably hard for a lot
of people outside of Georgia

00:10:05.705 --> 00:10:08.574
to understand exactly
what you explained.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:11.844
So Brian Kemp, our governor,
did something really well.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.413
When all the covid
shutdowns happened,

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.949
Georgia, and, sorry, Florida,

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:21.153
we were actually the first
state to reopen, thankfully.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.321
And that was something

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:24.490 align:start size:88% position:13%
I had talked with
Brian Kemp a lot about.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:27.193 align:start size:97% position:3%
I would call him, "Governor,
we've gotta reopen.

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:28.694
We need our schools reopened.

00:10:28.694 --> 00:10:30.630
Our businesses need
to be reopened."

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.298
You know, basically begging him.

00:10:32.298 --> 00:10:35.167 align:start size:88% position:13%
Thankfully Governor Kemp
listened to all of us

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:37.370 align:start size:84% position:16%
that were asking him
for these things.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
We reopened, so our
businesses got open again.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.108
People went back to work.

00:10:42.108 --> 00:10:43.776
Our kids weren't trapped at home

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:47.713
