00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:58.591
The Georgia is a big gun state.

00:10:58.591 --> 00:11:01.727
We have a lot of gun owners and
Second Amendment supporters.

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:03.829
So that was a critical
piece of legislation

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:05.364
that he got done.

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:08.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have a very strong
economy in Georgia.

00:11:08.034 --> 00:11:10.269 align:start size:97% position:3%
So these are the things that
people may forget about,

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:12.271
where they get caught
up in watching like,

00:11:12.271 --> 00:11:16.342 align:start size:88% position:13%
the President Trump,
Governor Kemp arguments.

00:11:16.342 --> 00:11:17.810
You know, those,

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
then those are really
more side stories instead-

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:21.247
- Because Trump did want
him to keep the stay closed

00:11:21.247 --> 00:11:22.848
longer than he did.

00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:24.016
- In the beginning, yeah.

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:26.352
That's what Dr. Fauci, Burkes,

00:11:26.352 --> 00:11:28.988
they were advising
President Trump.

00:11:28.988 --> 00:11:30.389
You can't fault President Trump.

00:11:30.389 --> 00:11:31.924
He was listening to the people

00:11:31.924 --> 00:11:33.893
that were supposed
to be the experts,

00:11:33.893 --> 00:11:36.929
and, yeah, he was telling
everybody to shut down.

00:11:36.929 --> 00:11:38.531
Brian Kemp reopened.

00:11:38.531 --> 00:11:41.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think there was a list
of others that reopened.

00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:44.970 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that shows you like
some of the reasons

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.272
kind of behind the scenes

00:11:46.272 --> 00:11:49.375
why people in Georgia
supported him so much

00:11:49.375 --> 00:11:50.876
in his reelection.

00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:52.511 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So why do you think the
Senate seats go the other way?

00:11:52.511 --> 00:11:55.347
- Well, I think it had
to do with candidates.

00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:57.983
I think it had to
do with campaigns.

00:11:57.983 --> 00:11:59.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
Another thing that
people may not realize

00:11:59.819 --> 00:12:03.422 align:start size:84% position:16%
is a campaign is
just like a business,

00:12:03.422 --> 00:12:05.257 align:start size:84% position:16%
and not all of
them do a good job.

00:12:05.257 --> 00:12:06.459
They really don't.

00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:08.494
There's a lot that
goes into a campaign.

00:12:08.494 --> 00:12:11.130
Its messaging is
really important.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:15.334 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's TV ads and placement,
radio ads and placement.

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:19.805
Social media is even just as
important as TV and radio,

00:12:19.805 --> 00:12:21.240
maybe even more so.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:25.511 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's your ground team,
door knocking, phone calls.

00:12:25.511 --> 00:12:27.780
I mean, it literally
is a mini business.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:30.316 align:start size:81% position:19%
And they don't
always do it well.

00:12:30.316 --> 00:12:34.620
Herschel Walker's campaign
was run by Washington DC,

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.223
wasn't run by people in Georgia

00:12:37.223 --> 00:12:41.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
that really understand
Republican Georgia voters.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.430
Mitch McConnell's
views and values

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.165
are not accepted in Georgia.

00:12:46.165 --> 00:12:50.169 align:start position:0%
And that proved to be true
with Kelly Loeffler's campaign.

00:12:50.169 --> 00:12:53.072
So when you have
team Mitch shirts

00:12:53.072 --> 00:12:55.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
going around in my
district, knocking doors,

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:57.409
that's not a good look

00:12:57.409 --> 00:12:59.278
for your Republican
senator's candidate.

00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:01.213
And that's just the truth.

00:13:01.213 --> 00:13:02.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Let me ask you a
couple of other things

00:13:02.848 --> 00:13:04.083
that you're sort of in
