that he's not doing enough.

00:16:28.187 --> 00:16:29.421
- Of course.

00:16:29.421 --> 00:16:30.923
- But nobody cared
about it before.

00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:32.157
But what about the people
on the government side?

00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:33.625
Whereas I kept saying
during the hearings,

00:16:33.625 --> 00:16:35.427 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's not that I have sympathy
for these Twitter people,

00:16:35.427 --> 00:16:37.196
but they're private employees

00:16:37.196 --> 00:16:39.999
who are maybe up to
no good, for sure.

00:16:39.999 --> 00:16:42.468
But they are also working
with government people.

00:16:42.468 --> 00:16:44.136
And it seems like we
still don't really know

00:16:44.136 --> 00:16:46.138
who those people are or
how high that goes up.

00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:47.773
- That is an extreme problem.

00:16:47.773 --> 00:16:49.808
So that's in Homeland Security.

00:16:49.808 --> 00:16:52.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, we know that
they are the ones

00:16:52.411 --> 00:16:55.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
that run these
disinformation programs

00:16:55.514 --> 00:16:59.585
in conjunction with the
FBI, the CIA and others.

00:16:59.585 --> 00:17:01.787
And so this is a
serious problem.

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:04.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's a weaponization
of government

00:17:04.089 --> 00:17:06.625
basically targeting our
First Amendment rights.

00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:09.528
There's a weaponization
of government committee.

00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:11.230 align:start size:84% position:16%
Jim Jordan is running
that committee.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:15.067 align:start size:97% position:3%
So we coordinate on
oversight under our chairman,

00:17:15.067 --> 00:17:17.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
Jamie Comer, and we
coordinate on these things,

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.438
but we were also-

00:17:19.438 --> 00:17:20.706
- And do you think you
can do anything on it?

00:17:20.706 --> 00:17:23.108
That's what everybody
always is, you know?

00:17:23.108 --> 00:17:24.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like, okay, you
have the hearing.

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.111
Does anyone pay the price?

00:17:26.111 --> 00:17:29.648 align:start position:0%
- Yeah, so I'm a business
owner, that's really what I was,

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:31.917
and a mom, I've got three kids,

00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:34.353
before I became a
member of Congress.

00:17:34.353 --> 00:17:36.655 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I know that money
is very powerful.

00:17:36.655 --> 00:17:38.524
So when you don't
pay for something,

00:17:38.524 --> 00:17:40.759
that means that it discontinues.

00:17:40.759 --> 00:17:42.361 align:start size:84% position:16%
So we've been
looking into things.

00:17:42.361 --> 00:17:45.431
I spoke with Jonathan
Turley last night,

00:17:45.431 --> 00:17:48.634 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he had a great suggestion
for us on oversight.

00:17:48.634 --> 00:17:51.703
But this also goes into our
budget and appropriations.

00:17:51.703 --> 00:17:54.606 align:start size:84% position:16%
The federal government
gives out grants.

00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:56.141
Okay, all kinds of grants,

00:17:56.141 --> 00:17:58.043
and that's a whole nother
topic we could talk about.

00:17:58.043 --> 00:18:00.579 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's a lot of grants
we have to cut out.

00:18:00.579 --> 00:18:03.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
But they give out grants
for disinformation.

00:18:03.549 --> 00:18:05.751
So this is basically tax dollars

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:09.021
funding all kinds of
groups, outside groups,

00:18:09.021 --> 00:18:10.789
and they spend all their
time, do, do, do, do, do,

00:18:10.789 --> 00:18:13.058 align:start size:84% position:16%
finding things they
want to censor.

00:18:13.058 --> 00:18:15.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then they would send them
to Homeland Security,

00:18:15.561 --> 00:18:18.263
send them to the
FBI and so forth.

00:18:18.263 --> 00:18:20.165
And then they come in,
and they funnel 'em down,

00:18:20.165 --> 00:18:21.567
and then, choo,
choo, choo, choo,

00:18:21.567 --> 00:18:23.702
wipe 'em off of
not just Twitter,

00:18:23.702 --> 00:18:26.138
which is actually one of the
smaller social media companies,

00:18:26.138 --> 00:18:29.241
Facebook, Instagram, on
the much bigger ones.

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:30.742
- Let me give you
one to look into,

00:18:30.742 --> 00:18:32.644
because this'll blow your mind
if you didn't hear about it.

00:18:32.644 --> 00:18:33.979
Do you know about News Guard?

00:18:33.979 --> 00:18:35.013
Have you heard about News Guard?

00:18:35.013 --> 00:18:36.482
- Uh-uh.

00:18:36.482 --> 00:18:37.749 align:start size:97% position:3%
So News Guard is one of
these, you know, nonprofits,

00:18:37.749 --> 00:18:40.786
which is funded by the
government, 750 grand.

00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:43.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had Marissa Streit,
she's the CEO of PragerU,

00:18:43.889 --> 00:18:45.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
which I'm sure
you're familiar with.

